A||||4||Rick 88||Door Adjustment  (Rattles over bumps with window down)||||5||
Z||000000||Rick 88||08-28-2001||05:40 PM||||My door striker pin has a small amount of surface wear. It rattles at the pin when the window is down. My door seals are good, the rubber bumper is intact, and the hinge pins are tight. Can the striker pin be adjusted or replaced? This only happens with the window down.<P>Rick <BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-28-2001||06:57 PM||||The door latch is probably worn. The window simply takes up some of the slop. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-28-2001||08:46 PM||||you can prob make it fit a little tighter my loosening the pin and moving it in towards interior. Take your time and make tiny movements, a little goes a long way. it screws into a trapped nutplate in jam and hole is larger than the pin so it will move up and down and in and out. You can also try getting it to catch in another spot on the pin by shimming it out from the jam or in by removing any that are already on it. when your done DONT slam it very hard till your sure it lines up or you can damage the latch in the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||08-29-2001||02:25 AM||||Thanks for the tip Roger. I adjusted the pin and the rattle is gone! It didn't take much, and sounds better when the door closes. I'm running out of rattles to fix.<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||6
Z||000004||3400Fiero||08-29-2001||01:45 PM||||uh, what's the striker pin?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||5
